<title>USA: Raytheon unit receives $500 million award.</title>
<headline>Raytheon unit receives $500 million award.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co 's Raytheon Engineers &amp; Constructors unit said on Tuesday it received a $500 million award to continue to operate the U.S. Army's chemical weapons destruction facility in the Pacific for the next five years.</p>
<p>Under the contract Raytheon will provide overall management of the facility as well as engineering, procurement and logistical support services.</p>
<p>Raytheon Engineers is an engineering, construction, operations and maintenance firm.</p>
